    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33832" root="فسح" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُسْحُمٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَسِيحٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ ٱبْنُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُسْحُمٍ</span> is a phrase mentioned by Lh, thought by
him to be from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفُسْحَةُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الاِنْفِسَاحُ</span>, but the
meaning is unknown. (L.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also The <i>glans
of the penis.</i> (K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فسحم</span>; where the word
is mentioned again in the S likewise.)

